  to define as a summary:
  
  Briefcase Builder defines what records are downloaded to the mobile device's encrypted SQLite store, 
  while the GraphQL wire adapter (lightning/uiGraphQLApi) defines how the LWC reads and queries that cached data without relying on an active network connection.
  We optimize this by keeping briefcase filters narrow—under 50,000 records—and using parameterized, static gql queries.
  
  Because queries are defined statically using the gql tag, Salesforce’s Mobile Offline runtime can statically analyze the exact fields, objects, and relationships requested.
  
  It pairs with Briefcase Builder to preload (prime) only the required data to the mobile device before the technician or rep goes offline.
  
  
