  By default, Book Appointment is standard on Work Orders, Work Order Line Items, and Service Appointments. However, enterprise workflows frequently require booking appointments directly from Opportunity, Case, Account, Lead, or Asset.
  
  There are two primary ways to implement this:
  
  Option A: Quick Action with Auto-Created Service Appointments (Declarative)
  Salesforce provides the standard Book Appointment quick action, which looks for an underlying Service Appointment.
  
  Flow Automation: When an action or milestone occurs on a standard object (e.g., Case reaches In Progress, or Opportunity reaches Proposal/Quote):
  
  Create a Work Order linking to the Case/Opportunity.
  
  Auto-generate a Service Appointment with default EarliestStartTimeAllowed and DueDate derived from the Parent.
  
  Expose Action: Add the standard Book Appointment quick action to the Page Layout of the Parent object (via related list or Lightning Action referencing the child SA).
  
  Option B: Programmatic Integration via FSL Global APIs (Apex / LWC)
  For custom objects, customer portals, or bespoke LWC flows, you can call the FSL Appointment Booking API directly from Apex without needing the standard UI modal.
  
  
